            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "maslex"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Have always loved these cookies and make them for Christmas each year. I take a can of cream cheese frosting (tint 1/2 with green and 1/2 with red food coloring) and then frost the cookies. MMMMMM"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "wim"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I’ve made these for years and everyone loves them. For the reviewers that found them bland. I agree. These are not sweet cookies so the flavors don’t pop. See they were made less sweet and a little dry so you can glob on loads of sweet buttery vanilla frosting. I think if the cookie was sweeter it might be too sweet with frosting.",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-22T23:35:44.126Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tammy Lynn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "They were puffy and very cakey. The taste is okay; I will let them sit and see if they are better in a couple days. I definitely had to put icing on them, otherwise they were not to our tastes.",
            "datePublished": "2021-01-04T19:35:29.567Z"
          },
          {
